CHAPTER.VERS:
What mean ye, that ye use this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying, 

          The people murmured at the chastising of the Lord, and therefore used this proverb meaning that their fathers had sinned and their children were punished for their transgressions. {{See Jer_31:29}}
         The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the children's teeth are set on edge?

Hath given forth upon interest, and hath taken increase: shall he then live? he shall not live: he hath done all these abominations; 

          He shows how the son is punished for his father's sin: that is, if he is wicked as his father was and does not repent, he will be punished as his father was, or else not.
         he shall surely die; his blood shall be upon him.
